       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum labeled daily dose for ibuprofen is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use in adults. This order is twice that.\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose, so 1600 mg is also double that limit.\n- **Risk:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up substantially. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for acute pain or inflammation. It's usually given with food, at the lowest effective dose and for the shortest duration.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours**, a common dose for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
