       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Ibuprofen at 6,400 mg/day is well above the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication where it's appropriate. Doses above 3,200 mg/day add toxicity without adding benefit. I'm not questioning your authority or your responsibility for the order. I just don't want to be the one to put an order in the system that I believe could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n- **Enter the maximum standard dose:** ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day).\n- **Enter a lower dose** if you give me one.\n- **Add a note** to the order, such as \"give with food\" or \"monitor renal function and GI symptoms.\"\n\nIf you think the patient needs more than 3,200 mg/day, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy or the attending first. If they approve a dose above the maximum, you can enter it directly through your hospital's override process.\n\nDo you want me to enter any of the options above?"
